      "findingMessages": {
        "p0002-ai-slop-misplaced-doc": "The doc comment that describes merge_undo (\"Fold the last `n` undo steps into one...\") is stacked on top of the doc for commits(), so rustdoc renders one run-on doc on Session::commits() and Session::merge_undo, the function it describes, has no doc at all. A reader of the generated docs or an agent reading the signature is told commits() folds undo steps.",
        "p0002-ai-slop-dead-param-pos": "The closure `one` in parse_gps takes a `pos: char` hemisphere letter (callers pass 'N' and 'E') that is never read; `let _ = pos;` only silences the unused warning. The positive hemisphere letter is therefore not validated: a latitude typed as \"51.5 E\" or a longitude as \"0.1 N\" is accepted silently as positive instead of rejected."
      },
      "findingTitles": {
        "p0002-ai-slop-misplaced-doc": "Move the \"Fold the last `n` undo steps into one\" paragraph down onto merge_undo and leave commits() with only its own \"How many undo steps were committed\" doc.",
        "p0002-ai-slop-dead-param-pos": "Either drop the `pos` parameter and the `let _ = pos;` suppression, or use it (reject a coordinate whose letter belongs to the other axis)."
      },
